# Vercel must not try to build a Python function out of this repo.
#
# The 5,715 MB bundle failure came from Vercel discovering a Python entry point
# and installing backend/requirements.txt, which pulls torch and its NVIDIA CUDA
# wheels. Nothing in here belongs on Vercel: the matching engine needs a
# persistent process, a warm FAISS index and PostgreSQL. Vercel hosts the
# offline console (one static HTML file) and nothing else.

backend/
api/
engine/
erp/
eval/
tests/
data/
docs/
*.py
requirements*.txt
Makefile
.env
.env.example
